t, but maybe we can adjust.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps this is close enough, and the error comes from rounding, and the minimal value is approximately achieved at these values.\n\nThen, compute xyz:\n\nxyz = 2^{S} * 3^{T}, where S = a + b + c and T = (1/2)a + (2/3)b + 2c.\n\nBut since we have M, N, P defined in terms of a, b, c, and M, N, P are related to a, b, c via:\n\nM = b + c + k(e + f) but e = (2/3)b and f = 2c, so M = b + c + k*(2/3 b + 2c) = b(1 + 2k/3) + c(1 + 2k)\n\nSimilarly, N = a + c + k*(d + f) = a + c + k*( (1/2)a + 2c ) = a(1 + k/2) + c(1 + 2k)\n\nP = a + b + k*(d + e) = a + b + k*( (1/2)a + (2/3)b ) = a(1 + k/2) + b(1 + 2k/3)\n\nBut since we have expressions for a, b, c in terms of M, N, P:\n\na = 8/M,\n\nb = 9/N,\n\nc = 5/P,\n\nTherefore,\n\nS = a + b + c = 8/M + 9/N + 5/P,\n\nT = (1/2)a + (2/3)b + 2c = (4/M) + (6/N) + 10/P\n\nThus,\n\nxyz = 2^{S} * 3^{T}\n\nWith S ≈ (8/7.118) + (9/7.118) + (5/4.616)\n\nWait no, S = a + b + c = 8/M + 9/N + 5/P ≈8/7.118 + 9/7.118 +5/4.616\n\nWait, since M=N≈7.118 and P≈4.616,\n\nSo,\n\na = 8/7.118 ≈1.125,\n\nb = 9/7.118 ≈1.265,\n\nc =5/4.616 ≈1.083,\n\nThus,\n\nS ≈1.125 +1.265 +1.083 ≈3.473,\n\nT = (1/2)a + (2/3)b + 2c ≈0.5625 + 0.843 + 2.166 ≈3.6715,\n\nThus,\n\nxyz ≈2^{3.473} * 3^{3.6715}\n\nCompute 2^3.473:\n\n2^3 =8, 2^0.473 ≈ e^{0.473 ln2} ≈ e^{0.473*0.693} ≈ e^0.328 ≈1.387\n\nThus 2^3.473 ≈8 *1.387≈11.096\n\n3^3.6715 = 3^3 * 3^0.6715 ≈27 * e^{0.6715 ln3} ≈27 * e^{0.6715*1.0986} ≈27 * e^{0.738} ≈27 *2.092≈56.484\n\nThus xyz ≈11.096 *56.484 ≈627.3\n\nHmm, approximately 627. But this is an approximation. The problem likely expects an exact answer, so perhaps my approach is wrong.\n\nAlternatively, maybe there's an exact solution.\n\nLet me consider that k = log₂3 is a constant, so let's treat it as a variable and see if the equations can be solved symbolically.\n\nRecall that we had:\n\nxyz = 2^{(M + N + P)/2}\n\nWe need to minimize this, so minimize M + N + P.\n\nFrom the earlier relationships when assuming M=N, 