2017 × 7\n\nTherefore, \\( 20 \\times 706 - 2017 \\times 7 = 1 \\).\n\nTherefore, the coefficient of 20 is 706, so \\( 20^{-1} \\mod 2017 \\) is 706, since \\( 20 \\times 706 \\equiv 1 \\mod 2017 \\).\n\nTherefore, \\( t \\equiv 2016 \\times 706 \\mod 2017 \\).\n\nNow, compute \\( 2016 \\times 706 \\mod 2017 \\).\n\nFirst, note that 2016 ≡ -1 mod 2017, so:\n\n\\( t \\equiv (-1) \\times 706 \\mod 2017 \\equiv -706 \\mod 2017 \\).\n\nBut -706 mod 2017 is 2017 - 706 = 1311.\n\nWait, let me verify that:\n\n2017 - 706 = 2017 - 700 - 6 = 1317 - 6 = 1311. Yes, so \\( t \\equiv 1311 \\mod 2017 \\).\n\nBut since \\( t \\) must be between 0 and 2016 (because \\( t < 2017 \\)), then \\( t = 1311 \\).\n\nTherefore, \\( t = 1311 \\).\n\nTherefore, recall that \\( r = t \\times k \\), but wait, no: wait, earlier we had \\( r = t \\times k \\), but actually, no. Wait, let's recap:\n\nWe had \\( r \\equiv 0 \\mod k \\), so \\( r = t \\times k \\), where \\( t \\) is an integer between 0 and 2016 (since \\( r < 2017 \\times k \\)), and also \\( r \\equiv -1 \\mod 2017 \\). Then, through substitution, we found that \\( t \\equiv 1311 \\mod 2017 \\), but since \\( t < 2017 \\), \\( t = 1311 \\). Therefore, \\( r = 1311 \\times k \\).\n\nTherefore, \\( r = 1311 \\times k \\), and \\( m = 2025! = 2017 \\times k \\), so \\( \\frac{r}{m} = \\frac{1311 \\times k}{2017 \\times k} = \\frac{1311}{2017} \\).\n\nTherefore, the value of \\( \\frac{r}{2025!} \\) is \\( \\frac{1311}{2017} \\).\n\nBut wait, hold on, let me check that again. Because \\( r = t \\times k \\), and \\( m = 2017 \\times k \\), so yes, \\( r/m = t / 2017 \\). Since \\( t = 1311 \\), then \\( r/m = 1311 / 2017 \\). So that is the fraction.\n\nBut let me confirm all steps once more to be sure.\n\nFirst, we set \\( m = 2025! \\), \\( a = 2017 \\), want \\( a^{m} - 1 \\mod m \\). Since \\( a \\) divides \\( m \\), so \\( \\gcd(a, m) = a \\). Then, by Chinese Remainder Theorem, since \\( m = 2017 \\times k \\), with \\( \\gcd(