ht not be helpful.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps try to substitute specific values for z.\n\nLet me suppose that z is a simple fraction, like 1/2,\n\nLet me try z=0.5,\n\nThen,\n\nCompute each term:\n\nFirst term: sqrt(2*(0.25)+1) * sqrt( (4*(0.25)+1)/3 )=sqrt(0.5 +1)=sqrt(1.5)*sqrt( (1 +1)/3 )=sqrt(1.5)*sqrt(2/3)=sqrt( (1.5)*(2/3) )=sqrt(1)=1,\n\nSecond term: 0.5 * sqrt( (1 +1)/3 )=0.5 * sqrt(2/3)≈0.5*0.8165≈0.408,\n\nThird term:0.5 * sqrt(2*(0.25)+1)=0.5*sqrt(1.5)≈0.5*1.2247≈0.612,\n\nTotal≈1 +0.408 +0.612≈2.02, which is too big.\n\nHmm, z=0.5 gives the same as k=5.\n\nAlternatively, z=0.2,\n\nThen,\n\nz=0.2 ⇒ t=0.04,\n\nFirst term: sqrt(2*(0.04)+1)*sqrt( (4*0.04 +1)/3 ) = sqrt(0.08 +1)=sqrt(1.08)*sqrt( (0.16 +1)/3 )=sqrt(1.08)*sqrt(1.16/3),\n\nCompute sqrt(1.08)≈1.039,\n\nsqrt(1.16/3)=sqrt(0.3867)≈0.622,\n\nSo first term≈1.039 *0.622≈0.645,\n\nSecond term:0.2*sqrt( (4*0.04 +1)/3 )=0.2*sqrt(1.16/3)=0.2*0.622≈0.124,\n\nThird term:0.2*sqrt(2*0.04 +1)=0.2*sqrt(1.08)≈0.2*1.039≈0.208,\n\nTotal≈0.645+0.124+0.208≈0.977, close to 1.\n\nHmm, z=0.2 gives total≈0.977,\n\nz=0.21,\n\nt=0.0441,\n\nFirst term: sqrt(2*0.0441 +1)*sqrt( (4*0.0441 +1)/3 )\n\nCompute 2*0.0441=0.0882,\n\nThus sqrt(1.0882)≈1.043,\n\nInside second sqrt: 4*0.0441=0.1764,\n\nSo (0.1764 +1)/3=1.1764/3≈0.3921,\n\nsqrt(0.3921)=0.626,\n\nThus first term≈1.043 *0.626≈0.652,\n\nSecond term:0.21 * sqrt( (4*0.0441 +1)/3 )=0.21*sqrt(1.1764/3)=0.21*sqrt(0.3921)=0.21*0.626≈0.131,\n\nThird term:0.21*sqrt(2*0.0441 +1)=0.21*sqrt(1.0882)=0.21*1.043≈0.219,\n\nTotal≈0.652 +0.131 +0.219≈1.002,\n\nSo at z=0.21, the total is≈1.002,\n\nTherefore, z≈0.21,\n\nThus, z≈0.21,\n\nThen, compute a,b,c:\n\nFirst, z=0.21,\n\nThen,\n\ny= sqrt( (4z² +1)/3 )=sqrt(4*(0.0441)+1)/3)=sqrt(0.1764 +1)/3)=sqrt(1.1764/3)=sqrt(0.3921)=0.626,\n\nThen x= sqrt(2z² +1)=sqrt(2*(0.0441)+1)=sqrt(1.0882)=≈1.043,\n\nThus,\n\na≈1.043,\n\nb≈0.626,\n\nc≈0.21,\n\nTherefore, a + b + c≈1.043 +0.626 +0.21≈1.879,\n\nSame as before.\n\nTherefore, the approximate value 