answer is 15/8,\n\nbut I need to verify.\n\nLet me check with k such that a + b + c = 15/8 = 1.875,\n\nthen, (a + b + c)^2 = (15/8)^2 = 225/64 ≈ 3.515625,\n\nFrom earlier, (a + b + c)^2 = (13k)/12 - 1,\n\nso,\n\n225/64 = (13k)/12 - 1,\n\nso,\n\n(13k)/12 = 225/64 + 1 = 225/64 + 64/64 = 289/64,\n\nThus,\n\nk = (289/64) * (12/13) = (289 * 12)/(64 * 13),\n\nCompute numerator: 289 * 12 = 289 * 10 + 289 * 2 = 2890 + 578 = 3468,\n\nDenominator: 64 * 13 = 832,\n\nThus,\n\nk = 3468 / 832,\n\nSimplify,\n\nDivide numerator and denominator by 4:\n\n3468 ÷ 4 = 867,\n\n832 ÷ 4 = 208,\n\nSo, k = 867 / 208 ≈ 4.1649,\n\nHmm, so k ≈ 4.1649,\n\nthen, compute ab + bc + ca with k = 4.1649,\n\nLet me compute a, b, c:\n\na = sqrt(4.1649/2 - 1) = sqrt(2.08245 - 1) = sqrt(1.08245) ≈ 1.0405,\n\nb = sqrt(4.1649/3 - 1) = sqrt(1.3883 - 1) = sqrt(0.3883) ≈ 0.623,\n\nc = sqrt(4.1649/4 - 1) = sqrt(1.0412 - 1) = sqrt(0.0412) ≈ 0.203,\n\nThen,\n\nab ≈ 1.0405 * 0.623 ≈ 0.649,\n\nbc ≈ 0.623 * 0.203 ≈ 0.1266,\n\nca ≈ 0.203 * 1.0405 ≈ 0.2114,\n\nTotal ≈ 0.649 + 0.1266 + 0.2114 ≈ 0.649 + 0.338 ≈ 0.987,\n\nHmm, which is less than 1,\n\nso k = 867/208 ≈ 4.1649 gives ab + bc + ca ≈ 0.987,\n\nwhich is close but not 1,\n\nso 15/8 may not be the exact answer.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps 13/7 ≈ 1.857,\n\nthen (13/7)^2 = 169/49 ≈ 3.449,\n\nso,\n\n(13k)/12 -1 = 169/49,\n\nthen,\n\n(13k)/12 = 169/49 + 1 = 169/49 + 49/49 = 218/49,\n\nso,\n\nk = (218/49)*(12/13) = (218*12)/(49*13) = 2616/637 ≈ 4.104,\n\nthen compute ab + bc + ca with k ≈4.104,\n\nthen,\n\na = sqrt(4.104/2 -1)=sqrt(2.052 -1)=sqrt(1.052)≈1.0256,\n\nb= sqrt(4.104/3 -1)=sqrt(1.368 -1)=sqrt(0.368)≈0.6066,\n\nc= sqrt(4.104/4 -1)=sqrt(1.026 -1)=sqrt(0.026)=0.1612,\n\nthen,\n\nab≈1.0256 *0.6066≈0.622,\n\nbc≈0.6066 *0.1612≈0.0978,\n\nca≈0.1612 *1.0256≈0.1655,\n\nTotal≈0.622+0.0978+0.1655≈0.885,\n\nstill below 1.\n\nHmm.\n\nAlternatively, maybe the answer is  sqrt( (13k)/12 - 1 ) and k is such that the equation holds, so unless there's a specific trick, maybe t