 a pattern here.\n\nIt seems that there are multiple minimal hitting sets of size 3, and each can be extended by adding any of the remaining nodes to form hitting sets of size 4. To count all unique hitting sets of size 4, we need to consider all minimal hitting sets of size 3 and then for each, add the remaining nodes not in the minimal hitting set.\n\nBut first, let's try to list all minimal hitting sets of size 3.\n\nFrom above, we have identified the following minimal hitting sets of size 3:\n\n1. {4,6,8}\n\n2. {4,5,6}\n\n3. {4,2,6}\n\n4. {4,2,8}\n\n5. {6,8,2}\n\nAdditionally, let's see if there are others.\n\nCheck {4,5,8}:\n\n- Path 1: includes 4, so hit.\n\n- Path 2: includes 4 and 5, so hit.\n\n- Path 3: includes 8, but not 5 or 6. Path 3 is 7-8-9-6-3. It includes 8 but not 5 or 6. Since the hitting set is {4,5,8}, path 3 is hit by 8. So yes.\n\n- Path 4: includes 5, so hit.\n\n- Longer paths: 7-4-5-8-9-6-3: includes 4,5,8, so hit.\n\n- 7-8-5-2-1-4-5-6-3: includes 4,5,8, so hit.\n\n- 7-8-5-6-9-6-3: includes 5 and 8, so hit.\n\nSo {4,5,8} is also a hitting set of size 3.\n\nSimilarly, {4,5,8} is another minimal hitting set.\n\nSimilarly, {4,5,2}?\n\nCheck {4,5,2}:\n\n- Path 1: includes 4 and 2, so hit.\n\n- Path 2: includes 4 and 5, so hit.\n\n- Path 3: includes 6? No. Path 3 is 7-8-9-6-3. It doesn't include 4,5, or 2. So path 3 is not hit by {4,5,2}. So no.\n\nHow about {5,6,8}?\n\n- Path 1: includes 6? No. Path 1 is 7-4-1-2-3, which doesn't include 5,6, or 8. So not hit. So no.\n\n{2,5,8}:\n\n- Path 1: includes 2, so hit.\n\n- Path 2: includes 5, so hit.\n\n- Path 3: includes 8, so hit.\n\n- Path 4: includes 2 and 5? Path 4 is 7-8-5-2-3, so yes, includes 5 and 2. So hit.\n\n- Longer paths: yes, as above.\n\nSo {2,5,8} is a hitting set of size 3.\n\nSimilarly, {2,5,6}?\n\n- Path 1: includes 2, so hit.\n\n- Path 2: includes 5 and 6, so hit.\n\n- Path 3: includes 6, so hit.\n\n- Path 4: includes 2 and 5, so hit.\n\n- Longer paths: yes.\n\nSo {2,5,6} is a hitting set of size 3.\n\nSimilarly, {2,5,4} we already had as {4,2,5}? Wait no, {4,2,5} wasn't listed before. Let me check {4,2,5}:\n\n- Path 1: includes 4 and 2, so hit.\n\n- Path 2: includes 4 and 5, so hit.\n\n- Path 3: includes 6? No. Path 3 is 7-8-9-6-3, so not hit by {4,2,5}. So no.\n\nTherefore, {4,2,5} is not a hitting set.\n\nContinuing, let's see {5,6,2} we already had as {2,5,6}.\n\nHow about {4,8,5} we saw earlier didn't work.\n\n{4,8,2} we had earlier as a hitting set.\n\nWait, {4,8,2} is the same as {2,4,8}, which we had.\n\nIs there a minimal hitting set like {5,8, something}?\n\n{5,8, something}:\n\nTake {5,8,6}: as above, path 1 isn't hit.\n\n{5,8,2}: which is {2,5,8}, which we already have.\n\n{5,8,4}: {4,5,8}, which we have.\n\nSo maybe that's all.\n\nLet me try to list all minimal hitting sets of size 3 that I can find:\n\n1. {4,6,8}\n\n2. {4,5,6}\n\n3. {4,2,6}\n\n4. {4,2,8}\n\n5. {6,8,2}\n\n6. {4,5,8}\n\n7. {2,5,8}\n\n8. {2,5,6}\n\nThat's eight minimal hitting sets of size 3.\n\nWait, let me verify each one:\n\n1. {4,6,8} – checked earlier, works.\n\n2. {4,5,6} – checked, works.\n\n3. {4,2,6} – checked, works.\n\n4. {4,2,8} – checked, works.\n\n5. {6,8,2} – checked, works.\n\n6. {4,5,8} – checked, works.\n\n7. {2,5,8} – checked, works.\n\n8. {2,5,6} – checked, works.\n\nAre there any others?\n\nHow about {4,5,2}? No, as above.\n\n{5,6,8}? Doesn't work.\n\n{4,6,5}? That's {4,5,6}, already listed.\n\n{4,8,5}? That's {4,5,8}, already listed.\n\n{2,6,8}? That's {6,8,2}, already listed.\n\n{2,4,5}? Doesn't work.\n\n{4,2,5}? Doesn't work.\n\n{5,6,2}? That's {2,5,6}, already listed.\n\n{4,8, something else?} {4,8,1}? Let's check {4,8,1}:\n\n- Path 1: includes 4, so hit.\n\n- Path 2: includes 4, so hit.\n\n- Path 3: includes 8, so hit.\n\n- Path 4: includes 8, so hit.\n\n- Longer paths: 7-4-5-8-9-6-3: includes 4,8, so hit.\n\n- 7-8-5-2-1-4-5-6-3: includes 4,8, so hit.\n\n- 7-4-5-2-1-4-5-6-3: includes 4, so hit.\n\nSo {4,8,1} is also a hitting set of size 3!