es 13}{4 \\times 3 \\times 2 \\times 1} = \\frac{16 \\times 15 \\times 14 \\times 13}{24}\n\\]\n\nCalculating numerator step by step:\n\n16 × 15 = 240\n\n240 × 14 = 3360\n\n3360 × 13 = 43680\n\nThen divide by 24: 43680 / 24 = 1820\n\nSo, \\(\\binom{16}{4} = 1820\\)\n\nThen, \\(\\binom{12}{4}\\):\n\n12 × 11 × 10 × 9 / 24\n\n12 × 11 = 132\n\n132 × 10 = 1320\n\n1320 × 9 = 11880\n\nDivide by 24: 11880 / 24 = 495\n\nSo, \\(\\binom{12}{4} = 495\\)\n\nNext, \\(\\binom{8}{4}\\):\n\n8 × 7 × 6 × 5 / 24\n\n8 × 7 = 56\n\n56 × 6 = 336\n\n336 × 5 = 1680\n\nDivide by 24: 1680 / 24 = 70\n\nSo, \\(\\binom{8}{4} = 70\\)\n\nThen, \\(\\binom{4}{4} = 1\\)\n\nSo, the numerator is 1820 × 495 × 70 × 1.\n\nLet me compute that step by step.\n\nFirst, compute 1820 × 495.\n\nHmm, let's break that down.\n\n1820 × 495 = 1820 × (500 - 5) = 1820 × 500 - 1820 × 5\n\n1820 × 500 = 910,000\n\n1820 × 5 = 9,100\n\nTherefore, 910,000 - 9,100 = 900,900\n\nSo, 1820 × 495 = 900,900\n\nThen, multiply that by 70:\n\n900,900 × 70\n\nWell, 900,900 × 7 = 6,306,300\n\nTherefore, 900,900 × 70 = 6,306,300 × 10 = 63,063,000\n\nWait, actually, no: 900,900 × 70 is equal to 900,900 × 7 × 10, so yes, 6,306,300 × 10 = 63,063,000.\n\nTherefore, the numerator is 63,063,000.\n\nThen, divide by 4! = 24.\n\nSo, total number of partitions is 63,063,000 / 24.\n\nCompute that:\n\n63,063,000 ÷ 24.\n\nDivide numerator and denominator by 12 first: 63,063,000 ÷ 12 = 5,252,250, and 24 ÷ 12 = 2, so now we have 5,252,250 ÷ 2 = 2,626,125.\n\nWait, let me check that division again.\n\nWait, 63,063,000 ÷ 24:\n\nFirst, 24 × 2,600,000 = 24 × 2,000,000 + 24 × 600,000 = 48,000,000 + 14,400,000 = 62,400,000.\n\nSubtract that from 63,063,000: 63,063,000 - 62,400,000 = 663,000.\n\nNow, 24 × 27,625 = ?\n\nWait, 24 × 27,000 = 648,000\n\n24 × 625 = 15,000\n\nSo, 24 × 27,625 = 24 × (27,000 + 625) = 648,000 + 15,000 = 663,000.\n\nTherefore, total is 2,600,000 + 27,625 = 2,627,625.\n\nWait, hold on, that contradicts my previous step. Wait, let me re-e