\n3x1 + √3 y1 = [225 +15√69 +75 -15√69]/24 = (225 +75)/24 = 300/24 =12.5\n\nThus,\n\nt=25 /12.5=2.\n\nBut t=2 would place P outside the triangle, since AO_circum is from (0,0) to (3, √3), so t=2 would be beyond the circumcenter.\n\nTherefore, this suggests that P is not on AO_circum.\n\nHmm.\n\nAlternatively, suppose that P is such that AP is perpendicular to AX. Since AX is a chord, and AP is the diameter, then the line AP is perpendicular to the tangent at X, but the tangent at X to the circumcircle is perpendicular to the radius O_circum X.\n\nThus, if AP is perpendicular to the tangent at X, then AP is parallel to the radius O_circum X.\n\nWait, the tangent at X is perpendicular to the radius O_circum X. So if AP is perpendicular to the tangent, then AP is parallel to O_circum X.\n\nThus, vector AP is parallel to vector O_circum X.\n\nIn coordinates, with A at (0,0), O_circum is at (3, √3), and X is at (x_X, y_X). So vector O_circum X is (x_X -3, y_X -√3).\n\nVector AP is (p, q).\n\nIf they are parallel, then (p, q) = k*(x_X -3, y_X -√3) for some scalar k.\n\nTherefore,\n\np =k(x_X -3),\n\nq =k(y_X -√3).\n\nAdditionally, since P lies on the line from A through the direction of O_circum X.\n\nAlso, the point P must satisfy the condition x1 p + y1 q =25.\n\nLet me substitute p and q:\n\nx1 *k(x_X -3) + y1 *k(y_X -√3) =25\n\nFactor out k:\n\nk[ x1(x_X -3) + y1(y_X -√3) ] =25\n\nCompute the expression in brackets:\n\nx1 x_X -3x1 + y1 y_X - y1 √3\n\nBut note that x1 and y1 are coordinates of X, so x1 x_X + y1 y_X = |X|²=25.\n\nThus,\n\n=25 -3x1 - y1 √3\n\nTherefore,\n\nk[25 -3x1 - y1 √3 ] =25 → k=25/[25 -3x1 - y1 √3 ]\n\nCompute denominator:\n\n25 -3x1 - y1 √3\n\nFrom earlier computations in the coordinate system with A at (0,0):\n\nFor X1:\n\nx1=(75 +5√69)/24,\n\ny1=(5√3)(5 -√69)/24\n\nThus,\n\n3x1 =3*(75 +5√69)/24 = (225 +15√69)/24,\n\ny1 √3 = [5√3*(5 -√69)/24] *√3 =5*(3)*(5 -√69)/24 =15*(5 -√69)/24\n\nThus,\n\nDenominator:\n\n25 - [ (225 +15√69)/24 +15*(5 -√69)/24