mpute them exactly.\n\nLet me attempt to compute them exactly.\n\nLet me denote z = X = x + yi,\n\nthen,\n\n|z| = 5 ⇒ x² + y² = 25,\n\nand |z - (3 + √3 i)| = 2√3 ⇒ (x - 3)^2 + (y - √3)^2 = (2√3)^2 = 12.\n\nExpand the second equation:\n\nx² - 6x + 9 + y² - 2√3 y + 3 = 12,\n\nSimplify:\n\nx² + y² - 6x - 2√3 y + 12 = 12,\n\nThus,\n\nx² + y² - 6x - 2√3 y = 0,\n\nBut since x² + y² = 25,\n\nsubstitute:\n\n25 - 6x - 2√3 y = 0 ⇒ 6x + 2√3 y = 25,\n\nwhich is exactly the equation we had earlier for the coordinates of X.\n\nTherefore, the solutions for X are the same as we found before,\n\nand correspond to the two points,\n\none of which is inside the triangle and one outside.\n\nGiven that P is inside the triangle,\n\nprobably the X inside the triangle is the correct one,\n\nbut when we considered that case,\n\nit led to AP = 5,\n\nwhich is impossible.\n\nBut perhaps in complex numbers,\n\nthe coordinates of P can be expressed in terms of X,\n\nsince X lies on the circle with diameter AP,\n\nso in complex numbers,\n\nthe condition is that (X - p/2) * conjugate(X - p/2) = (|p|/2)^2,\n\nbut this might not help.\n\nAlternatively,\n\nsince in complex numbers,\n\nthe circle with diameter AP has center at p/2,\n\nand radius |p|/2,\n\nso any point X on this circle satisfies:\n\n|X - p/2| = |p|/2,\n\nwhich implies that X lies on the circle with center p/2 and radius |p|/2,\n\nso the equation is |X - p/2| = |p|/2,\n\nwhich simplifies to |X - p/2|² = |p|²/4,\n\nExpanding,\n\n(X - p/2)(\\overline{X} - \\overline{p}/2) = |p|²/4,\n\nMultiplying out,\n\nX \\overline{X} - (X \\overline{p} + \\overline{X} p)/2 + |p|²/4 = |p|²/4,\n\nThus,\n\n|X|² - (X \\overline{p} + \\overline{X} p)/2 = 0,\n\nBut X \\overline{p} + \\overline{X} p = 2 Re(X \\overline{p}),\n\nso,\n\n|X|² - Re(X \\overline{p}) = 0,\n\nTherefore,\n\nRe(X \\overline{p}) = |X|²,\n\nSince |X| = 5,\n\nthis becomes,\n\nRe(X \\overline{p}) = 25,\n\nBut X and p are complex numbers,\n\nso X \\overline{p} = X (x - yi) if p = x + yi,\n\n