9,\n\nCorrect.\n\nTherefore, the calculation is correct, and the discrepancy must be due to an error in the previous assumption that the order of the points was correct for the shoelace formula.\n\nWait, in the symbolic calculation, I used the order O1, O2, O3, O4, but perhaps the correct order is different?\n\nWait, in the symbolic calculation, I used the same order as before: O1, O2, O3, O4.\n\nBut according to approximate coordinates, this should be the correct order for a convex quadrilateral.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps the correct order is O1, O2, O3, O4 but the shoelace formula requires the points to be ordered clockwise or counter-clockwise without crossing.\n\nLet me check the ordering with the exact coordinates:\n\nO1: (5.5, ~18.2),\n\nO2: (8.5, ~12.77),\n\nO3: (8.5, ~4.26),\n\nO4: (~2.77, ~2.79),\n\nPlotting these points, the order O1-O2-O3-O4-O1 should form a convex quadrilateral.\n\nHowever, when applying the shoelace formula with this order, we obtained Area =6239√15⁄440≈14.18045√15≈54.9,\n\nWhereas when I computed via the first method with the correct arithmetic, I got 156√15⁄11≈14.1818√15≈54.9,\n\nAnd 6239/440≈14.18045,\n\nThe difference is minimal and likely due to rounding in the approximate calculations, but symbolically, they should be equal if there's no error.\n\nWait, 6239/440 simplifies to:\n\nDivide numerator and denominator by GCD(6239,440).\n\nFind GCD(6239,440):\n\nCompute GCD(440,6239 mod 440),\n\n6239 ÷440=14×440=6160, remainder 6239-6160=79,\n\nThus GCD(440,79),\n\n440 ÷79=5×79=395, remainder 45,\n\nGCD(79,45),\n\n79 ÷45=1×45=45, remainder 34,\n\nGCD(45,34),\n\n45 ÷34=1×34=34, remainder 11,\n\nGCD(34,11),\n\n34 ÷11=3×11=33, remainder 1,\n\nGCD(11,1)=1,\n\nThus GCD is 1,\n\nTherefore, 6239/440 is reduced.\n\nSimilarly, 156/11 is reduced.\n\nTherefore, unless there's an error in the symbolic calculation, the exact area is 6239√15⁄440,\n\nBut this contradicts the earlier method where I had:\n\nAfter correcting the arithmetic mistake, got 62